Greetings.

Enclosed with this email is the source code that goes
with the JOOP article entitled:

"A Pictorial Design Notation for Software-ICs."         

published in the July/Aug 1990 Issue (Vol 3, No2).  I
hope it proves useful for taking a look at an alternate
approach for structuring Objective-C based apps.  

A second set of source will follow at a later time.  This
is the source from the sample application in the second
edition of "Object-Oriented Programming: An Evolutionary
Approach" (Cox & Novobilski) in Chapter nine.  Unfortunatly,
it requires ICpak 201 to completely build, but what the
heck, it might help.

As I mentioned in the README file, I'm open to discussions
on the form and reasoning behind what was done, but not
really interested in providing help on porting this to
other platforms.  My apologizes for taking so long to       
provide this code, but my boss found something to do with
the free time I thought I had after completing my last
project.  Oh well .....

